  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-06-30T10:54:06.627Z",
  "deleteID": null,
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I would like to request an optional creator-controlled avatar visibility setting that allows avatar owners to show their full avatar only to selected viewer groups, while everyone else sees the avatar’s generated Impostor instead.\n\nSuggested setting:\n\n- Full Avatar Visible To: Everyone / Friends / Friends + Groups / Invite-only list / Nobody\n\n- All Other Viewers See: Generated Impostor or Fallback\n\n- Owner View: Always sees their own full avatar\n\n- Friend View: Can see the full avatar if permitted by the avatar owner’s setting\n\n- Non-Friend View: Loads only the Impostor instead of the full avatar\n\nThe main goal is creator protection and privacy. Many avatar creators want to use high-effort personal or commissioned avatars in public worlds, but they do not want to expose the full avatar asset to every nearby user. Current avatar protection methods are mostly Unity-side workarounds, shader obfuscation, or mesh scrambling, and they can be fragile, performance-heavy, or uncomfortable for legitimate users.\n\nA native VRChat-side visibility policy would be much cleaner:\n\n1. Non-friends can still recognize the user through the Impostor.\n\n2. Friends can still see the full avatar normally.\n\n3. Creators get a safer way to use personal avatars in public instances.\n\n4. Public worlds become less risky for people using private, commissioned, or unreleased avatars.\n\n5. It could reduce the need for aggressive third-party anti-rip systems.\n\nFor this to meaningfully protect creators, the full avatar asset should ideally not be downloaded or loaded by clients that are only allowed to see the Impostor. If the full avatar bundle is still delivered to non-friends, the feature would be useful for privacy and presentation, but much weaker as creator protection.\n\nThis should be optional and per-avatar or per-user, not forced globally. It should also respect existing Safety Settings, avatar hiding, blocking, platform compatibility, and performance systems.\n\nA possible UI label could be:\n\n“Show full avatar to: Everyone / Friends / Selected Groups”\n\n“Show Impostor to everyone else”\n\nThis would make Impostors more useful beyond platform fallback and performance cases, while giving creators a first-party, non-destructive way to protect private avatars.",
